{
 "module": "scene",
 "storyboard": "films/scene/product-feature-tour.storyboard.md",
 "_template": "FILLABLE TEMPLATE - a dark, chaptered product tour. Three numbered chapters (intake, plan, build), a proof number, an end card. Nothing here is anyone's brand: the product is the fictional 'Northwind', every colour is a theme token, and the end mark is an inline svg that draws itself. To reskin, change `theme` and nothing else. To refill, replace the copy, the board cards, the three roadmap bars, the agent transcript and the adoption count. Structure, timing and the chapter rhythm are the part worth keeping.",
 "orientation": "landscape",
 "theme": "northwind",
 "duration": 50,
 "_sceneUnits": "OFF deliberately. A cut film with no choreographed motion track gets beat wrapping by default (core/produce.js), and this film has layers that outlive their own beat: the roadmap bars, their beams and the agent-panel captions. Wrapping truncated five of them and held five others open past the duration the JSON states. The cuts transform the root instead, and every layer keeps the window it was written with.",
 "sceneUnits": false,
 "_camera": "The camera is written as MOVES, not keys: core/camera-moves.js owns the arithmetic, so retiming a chapter is one number. The dive is the only large one, and it lands on the agent panel because chapter 3 is what the film is arguing. A dive is bounded by the copy it must not push off the frame. At scale s centred on tx the left edge of the visible stage is tx - 960/s, and both films set their text column at x=150, so tx must stay at or under 150 + 960/s. The first pass dove to 1.2 on the panel centre and cropped the whole left column for five seconds with every gate green; `make judge` was the only thing that saw it.",
 "_cuts": "The MOTION family, which is what the motion director picks for this theme's punchy personality, rotated across its members. A matte cut (wipe, iris, blinds) would have matched the three roadmap bars, but core/cuts.js refuses one on a whole-frame root and the only way to earn it is beat wrapping, which this film opts out of one field up. So the film carries two cut families: shape inside the beat, motion between them. Each cut sits on a chapter boundary, and the backdrop windows at the foot of the file carry no times because they bind to these joints (core/junctions.js).",
 "spectacle": {
  "at": 34.4,
  "of": "adoptionCount",
  "device": "streak",
  "why": "Three chapters have followed ONE issue from an inbox to a merged change. The peak lands where the counter stops rather than at the cut, so the sting punctuates the finished figure instead of covering it while it counts. It is the only beat allowed to raise its voice."
 },
 "audio": {
  "silent": true,
  "_why": "Template ships mute so a fork can drop its own bed in without fighting a mix it did not choose. Replace with a real audio block before shipping."
 },
